 "reports_individuals_with_tnfaip3_variant": true,
 "relevance_note": "A narrative review of autoinflammatory skin diseases; its only individual-level Blau syndrome content is the Fig. 6 legend describing two boys ('A) A 12-year-old boy' and '(B) A 4-year-old boy').",
 "method_note": "Built by hand with a short script from my reading of the paper. The paper is a narrative review with no patient tables and no supplementary material; Table I gives disease-level summaries only (no individuals). The only in-scope people are the two boys in the Fig. 6 legend headed 'Blau syndrome.', labelled 'unnamed person 1' (panel A) and 'unnamed person 2' (panel B) under rule 6 (no paper labels; not a case report; not attributed to a reference). The paper prints no NOD2 variant for either boy and does not state that they were genetically tested, so the variants table is empty; their diagnosis is taken from the figure heading. Ages in the legend are taken as age at the time of the photograph/report (last evaluation). For unnamed person 2, 'joint involvement with cystic swelling' was recorded as the checklist item 'arthritis or joint synovitis' observed; tenosynovitis was left not reported because the paper does not name it. Disease-level statements (e.g. 'The main clinical characteristics are arthritis, skin inflammation and uveitis') are not about named individuals and were not used. No contradictions found.",
